{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cee47pus3Fvypsh19dQdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: needs_more_evidence\nCONSENSUS_BLOCKING: yes\nRATIONALE: The corrected two-file reconstruction is mechanically sound on every scenario that has a trusted receipt (normal push, corrected zero-base, deletion, invalid base, missing topic, HTTP-red semantics, protected-touch-never-red). But the merge-commit adjudication is TESTIMONY only: no trusted probe covers a merge commit whose protected change exists only in the merge itself (evil merge / conflict resolution). `protectedPathsForCommit` relies on `git diff-tree --first-parent` producing a first-parent diff for merge commits; plain `diff-tree` suppresses merge diffs entirely without `-m`/`-c`/`--diff-merges`, and whether `--first-parent` alone implies `--diff-merges=first-parent` in diff-tree single-commit mode is exactly the kind of git-version behavior that must be receipted, not assumed. If it does not, a merge commit touching a protected file only in its own diff is a silent detection miss — a totality violation of \"inspect every commit independently.\" Two lesser un-receipted edges: (a) orphan branch push (no merge-base with default) goes red as malfunction rather than detecting — conforms to malfunction-red but is un-receipted; (b) first-ever push of the default branch yields merge-base==head → commits=0 → silent empty range over the initial history. Neither of these alone blocks, but the merge-commit gap does until receipted.\nDISAGREEMENT: The prior adjudication statement \"Merge commits … are separate touching-commit/event detections, not approval blocks. No production correction was made\" is asserted without any trusted merge-commit probe. I challenge the implicit claim that `diff-tree --root --first-parent --name-only -r <merge-sha>` emits the first-parent diff for a merge commit; the receipt set contains zero merge-commit evidence.\nREQUIRED_RECHECK: Trusted-path probe: construct (or locate) a merge commit M in this repo where a protected file (e.g., `.claude/x` or `config/trading.config.json`) is modified in M's diff versus its first parent but in none of the non-merge commits of the scanned range; run `node scripts/check-protected-paths.js <M^> <M>` with NTFY_TOPIC unset and confirm touching=1 unavailable=1. Additionally run raw `git diff-tree --root --first-parent --no-commit-id --name-only -r -z <M>` and show non-empty output on the runner's git version.\nRECHECK_PROMPT: \"Provide a host-attested receipt for merge-commit detection: pick or synthesize a merge commit M whose first-parent diff modifies a protected path (including an evil-merge case where no constituent non-merge commit touches it). Run `git diff-tree --root --first-parent --no-commit-id --name-only -r -z M` and `node scripts/check-protected-paths.js M^ M` with NTFY_TOPIC unset; report git version, raw diff-tree output, exit code, and the commits/touching/delivered/unavailable line. Also receipt the orphan-branch zero-base case (merge-base failure) and state whether red-malfunction there is the intended disposition.\"\nNEXT_CHECK: `git --version && git diff-tree --root --first-parent --no-commit-id --name-only -r <[REDACTED]>` on the actual runner image — empty output on a protected-touching merge is the break.\nCANDIDATE SET: examined 2 of 2 touched files, plus all supplied evidence. Enumerated: scripts/check-protected-paths.js (runGit, isProtectedPath, verifyCommit, commitsInRange, protectedPathsForCommit, commitDetails, notificationBody, sendNotification, reportMalfunction, main, top-level catch); .github/workflows/protected-paths.yml (checkout fetch-depth 0, node 20, push step with 3-arg invocation, PR step with 2-arg invocation, NTFY_TOPIC secret env, contents:read); 10 trusted receipts (pre-fix commits=2026/touching=115, post-fix zero-base commits=1, missing-default red, deletion commits=0, MODULE_NOT_FOUND red, 3727b75d touching=1, 4ac6d010 touching=0, invalid-base red, node --check/git diff --check/language scan, Acorn parse); scenario candidates: normal push, PR, new branch, new branch off feature branch (duplicate re-notification), orphan branch, first-push-of-default, branch deletion, force-push, tag push, merge commit, evil merge, rename/delete of protected file, whitespace topic, HTTP 3xx/4xx/5xx/timeout/mid-stream abort.\nAST EVIDENCE: No AST tools available in this pass (named absence). Relying on host-attested trusted Acorn parse: commitsInRange def L47/call L176; protectedPathsForCommit def L75/call L187; commitDetails def L92/call L194; notificationBody def L106/call L201; sendNotification def L117/call L201; process.env.NTFY_TOPIC read L118; parse of full 221-line file with no syntax failure. Env keys touched: NTFY_TOPIC only (script L118, workflow both steps) — consistent with \"existing NTFY_TOPIC only.\"\nINHERITED: scripts/check-protected-paths.js — `String(process.env.NTFY_TOPIC || '')` is a `|| ''` env-read fallback, but it funnels into a named absence receipt rather than a silent default (noted, acceptable, unfixed); `result.stderr || result.stdout || 'no command output'` is a message-only fallback (benign, unfixed); no swallowed catches — every catch resolves to a red malfunction path. .github/workflows/protected-paths.yml — no inherited defaults; `origin/${{ …default_branch }}` interpolation is repo-owner-controlled (unfixed, low risk).\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 9 of 9. (1) missing base/head args → true boundary, red. (2) ZERO_SHA head (deletion) → unreachability-receipted (deletion receipt commits=0), green. (3) `!newBranchBase` guard → producer-fixable defense (workflow always supplies arg), red on breach. (4) verifyCommit head/base/default checks → true boundary, red. (5) merge-base failure → true boundary, red (orphan-branch disposition un-receipted). (6) runGit spawn/status wrapping → true boundary, red. (7) NTFY_TOPIC-absent fallback → true boundary with named absence, green non-silent (receipted). (8) HTTP non-2xx/timeout/socket-error → true boundary, red (receipted only as spec, not live). (9) main().catch → true boundary, red.\nALLEGATIONS: (A) Merge-commit/evil-merge silent-miss risk via diff-tree merge-suppression — SUBSTANTIVE, TESTIMONY-gapped (code RECEIPT shows the flag choice; absence of probe is the allegation) — this drives the recheck, not found_break, because code at HEAD is consistent with correct behavior on modern git. (B) First-push-of-default empty range — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT (code logic), theoretical scope. (C) Orphan-branch red instead of detect — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT, conforms to malfunction-red. (D) Cross-event duplicate notifications (branch created off feature branch, PR re-runs) — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT, consistent with per-invocation cardinality reading. (E) No live delivery receipt — correctly not claimed by the submission.\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY on allegation (A) merge-commit detection. Mercury seat: not selected (account inactive) — no quote available. Fable seat (this): \"diff-tree without -m/-c suppresses merge diffs; --first-parent's implication of --diff-merges=first-parent in single-commit diff-tree mode is unproven here; an evil merge touching a protected file could pass silently — receipt required before green.\" Kimi seat: not present in this evidence bundle — no quote available. Panel quorum on this point cannot converge without the demanded probe; Trey rules after the receipt lands.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: Full verbatim host-attested script (221 lines) and workflow (40 lines) with SHA-256 manifest; all 10 trusted receipts; Acorn AST line references; prior adjudication narrative (zero-base correction, force-push disposition, merge-commit disposition); path-matcher fidelity against the five protected globs; red/green branch inventory of main(); HTTP promise resolution paths including double-resolve safety.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: Actual repo state at 4ac6d010 (no