 sendNotification def L117/call L201; process.env.NTFY_TOPIC read L118; parse of full 221-line file with no syntax failure. Env keys touched: NTFY_TOPIC only (script L118, workflow both steps) — consistent with \"existing NTFY_TOPIC only.\"\nINHERITED: scripts/check-protected-paths.js — `String(process.env.NTFY_TOPIC || '')` is a `|| ''` env-read fallback, but it funnels into a named absence receipt rather than a silent default (noted, acceptable, unfixed); `result.stderr || result.stdout || 'no command output'` is a message-only fallback (benign, unfixed); no swallowed catches — every catch resolves to a red malfunction path. .github/workflows/protected-paths.yml — no inherited defaults; `origin/${{ …default_branch }}` interpolation is repo-owner-controlled (unfixed, low risk).\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 9 of 9. (1) missing base/head args → true boundary, red. (2) ZERO_SHA head (deletion) → unreachability-receipted (deletion receipt commits=0), green. (3) `!newBranchBase` guard → producer-fixable defense (workflow always supplies arg), red on breach. (4) verifyCommit head/base/default checks → true boundary, red. (5) merge-base failure → true boundary, red (orphan-branch disposition un-receipted). (6) runGit spawn/status wrapping → true boundary, red. (7) NTFY_TOPIC-absent fallback → true boundary with named absence, green non-silent (receipted). (8) HTTP non-2xx/timeout/socket-error → true boundary, red (receipted only as spec, not live). (9) main().catch → true boundary, red.\nALLEGATIONS: (A) Merge-commit/evil-merge silent-miss risk via diff-tree merge-suppression — SUBSTANTIVE, TESTIMONY-gapped (code RECEIPT shows the flag choice; absence of probe is the allegation) — this drives the recheck, not found_break, because code at HEAD is consistent with correct behavior on modern git. (B) First-push-of-default empty range — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT (code logic), theoretical scope. (C) Orphan-branch red instead of detect — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT, conforms to malfun